1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:02,188
You'd think the cure for a snakebite would

2
00:00:02,209 --> 00:00:02,981
be anything but a snake.

3
00:00:04,737 --> 00:00:06,841
God put a bronze one on a pole and said look.

4
00:00:08,543 --> 00:00:09,213
Not medicine.

5
00:00:10,421 --> 00:00:11,793
Not an antidote for the wound.

6
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:15,055
Just a look at the thing that was killing them.

7
00:00:17,202 --> 00:00:19,736
"Make thee a fiery serpent, and set it upon

8
00:00:19,777 --> 00:00:22,797
a pole: and it shall come to pass, that every

9
00:00:22,877 --> 00:00:24,857
one that is bitten, when he looketh upon it,

10
00:00:25,058 --> 00:00:25,561
shall live

11
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:29,690
if a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld

12
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:32,193
the serpent of brass, he lived." Call it strange

13
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:32,533
if you like.

14
00:00:33,259 --> 00:00:35,762
But God chose the exact shape of their death

15
00:00:36,022 --> 00:00:37,802
to become the shape of their life.

16
00:00:39,258 --> 00:00:42,697
We keep reaching for our own cure our own effort.

17
00:00:43,442 --> 00:00:46,479
God hung the remedy in plain sight and asked

18
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,559
only that we look.

19
00:00:48,988 --> 00:00:51,520
The cure was always shaped like the curse,

20
00:00:52,164 --> 00:00:54,547
lifted up and so was Christ.

21
00:00:55,856 --> 00:00:58,854
Look at what was lifted up for you, and live.
